# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage
/test-results/
/playwright-report/
/.lighthouseci/

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*

# vercel
.vercel

# local mission/artifact data — real user data from running OPTIMUS locally,
# never something to ship in the repo. Suffixed variant is the e2e suite's
# own isolated copy (playwright.config.ts), never the real one.
/.optimus-data*

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts
.rules-staged/
!.env.example

# All README.md files, everywhere in the repo — none of them ship. Kept on
# disk (source of documentation truth for whoever's absorbing a repo), just
# not committed. Explicit user call: don't publish internal build docs in a
# public repo. Matches every depth, so no per-directory drift is possible.
README.md
**/README.md
